{
  "critique": "The layout suffers from severe spatial conflict and hierarchy issues. The 'World Selector' and 'Progress' panels are awkwardly floating over the bottom level preview, obscuring the gameplay storytelling and creating a cluttered, unpolished look. The 'Hero' (bee) is visually disconnected from the level, hovering in a UI box rather than standing on the terrain, which breaks the 'mascot platformer' immersion. The 'Start Adventure' button, while prominent, is isolated from the visual narrative. The typography is strong, but the overall composition feels like a dashboard rather than a cohesive game launch screen. The 'distant goal' mentioned in the brief is barely visible or non-existent in the background, weakening the gameplay storytelling. The color palette is bright but lacks the 'depth' requested; the background is a flat gradient rather than a layered parallax scene.",
  "suggestion": "1. Restructure the layout to a clear 3-column or 2-row grid: Left (Title/CTA), Center (Hero + Level Preview), Right (Stats/Controls). 2. Integrate the Hero directly onto the level preview terrain, removing the floating UI box around it to create a seamless scene. 3. Move the World Selector to a dedicated horizontal strip below the level preview or into the right-hand sidebar to stop it from occluding the game world. 4. Enhance the level preview with distinct parallax layers (background hills, mid-ground platforms, foreground details) to satisfy the 'depth' requirement. 5. Add a visible 'Goal' (flag/portal) at the far right of the level preview to complete the narrative arc. 6. Refine the 'Start Adventure' button to be the primary visual anchor, perhaps placing it centrally below the level preview or integrated into the hero's starting position."
}
